### 2. Kani $2^e$-Gluing / Genus-2 Richelot Smooth-Isogeny Transfer over $\mathbb{F}_{\ell^2}$
- **Target $T$ & reduction:** For $N = pq$ with $p \equiv q \equiv 1 \pmod 3$ (general $N$: try $O(\log N)$ small discriminants $-D$ with $(-D/N) = +1$, [tracedata_results.md:220-248](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/tracedata_results.md#L220-L248)), find the two inequivalent norm-$N$ CM endomorphisms $\nu_+ = \pi_p \pi_q$ and $\nu_- = \pi_p \bar{\pi}_q$ in $\mathcal{O}_K = \mathbb{Z}[\omega]$ ($\omega^2 + \omega + 1 = 0$) of $E_0: y^2 = x^3 + 1$.
  - **Direction & cost [$T \equiv_R \text{FACT}$, PROVED]:** $\nu_+ \bar{\nu}_- = p \pi_q^2$, so $\gcd(\text{Re}_\omega(\nu_+ \bar{\nu}_-), \text{Im}_\omega(\nu_+ \bar{\nu}_-), N) \in \{p, q\}$ deterministically factors $N$ in $O(\log^2 N)$ bit-ops (checking the 6 unit associates of $\nu_-$; cf. [factorbits_results.md:273](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/factorbits_results.md#L273), [conn_alg.md:129](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/conn_alg.md#L129)). Thus $T$ at $L_N[\alpha]$ gives `FACT` at $L_N[\alpha]$.
- **Easy regime / free $N$-structure:** Polynomial-time SIDH torsion-isogeny break and Clapoti smooth-degree embedding (Castryck–Decru 2022; Robert 2023 [KNOWN]). Unlike $\pi_p$ (unknown degree $p$), **$\nu_\pm$ has PUBLIC degree $N$**! Pick a tiny norm $m = c_1^2 - c_1 c_2 + c_2^2 = \tilde{O}(\log^2 N)$ ($m = |\mu|^2$) and odd $e = \lceil \log_2(mN) \rceil + O(1)$ so $a = 2^e - mN$ is **prime $\equiv 1 \pmod 3$** [HEURISTIC: Bateman–Horn]; Cornacchia solves $|\alpha|^2 = a$ ($\alpha \in \mathbb{Z}[\omega]$) in $\text{poly}(\log N)$ time *without factoring*. Because $\mathbb{Z}[\omega]$ is commutative, Kani's matrix $F_{\nu'} = \begin{pmatrix} \alpha & \bar{\nu}' \\ -\nu' & \bar{\alpha} \end{pmatrix}$ ($\nu' = \mu \nu_\pm$) satisfies $F_{\nu'}^\dagger F_{\nu'} = 2^e I_2$ on **$E_0^2$ (genus $g = 2$!)**. Now choose a prime $\ell = c \cdot 2^{e+2} - 1 > 4mN$ ($\ell \equiv 2 \pmod 3$): over the **known field $\mathbb{F}_{\ell^2}$** (zero-divisor-free!), $E_0$ is supersingular with $E_0[2^{e+2}] \subset E_0(\mathbb{F}_{\ell^2})$ completely rational, every endomorphism of $E_0/\mathbb{F}_{\ell^2}$ of degree $< \ell/4$ lies strictly in $\mathbb{Z}[\omega]$ [PROVED], and each candidate $\tilde{\nu} \in \mathcal{T}_e := \{ u_0 + v_0 \omega \bmod 2^e : u_0^2 - u_0 v_0 + v_0^2 \equiv mN \pmod{2^e} \}$ ($|\mathcal{T}_e| = 3 \cdot 2^{e-1} \asymp N$) defines a smooth $e$-step genus-2 Richelot $(2,2)$-isogeny walk from $E_0^2$ whose codomain splits as $E_0^2$ (matching $\alpha$ on $E_0[3]$) **iff** $\tilde{\nu} = \mu \nu_\pm \pmod{2^e}$!
- **Why repo barriers do not apply:**
  - Evades `factorbits` PT ([factorbits_results.md:303-358](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/factorbits_results.md#L303-L358)), `nonsmooth` FROB ([nonsmooth_results.md:313-357](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nonsmooth_results.md#L313-L357)), and `conn_cmp` §4.1–4.2 ([conn_cmp.md:121-122](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/conn_cmp.md#L121-L122)) by working over the known prime-square field $\mathbb{F}_{\ell^2}$ rather than $\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$, and evades `genusleak` §4.1's CM bottleneck ([genusleak_results.md:404-421](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/genusleak_results.md#L404-L421)) by using fixed $j = 0$ curve $E_0$ instead of discriminant $-4N$. Evades `selfred` SR1/SR2 ([selfred_results.md:34-53](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/selfred_results.md#L34-L53)) via the *additive* split $2^e = a + mN$.
- **Ledger & steering cost:** Setup ($\ell$, $E_0[2^e](\mathbb{F}_{\ell^2})$, $\alpha$) costs $\text{poly}(\log N)$. Brute-forcing $\mathcal{T}_e$ costs $\tilde{O}(N)$ Richelot chains; algebraic elimination on the $e$ Boolean bits of $t \in \mathcal{T}_e$ for the Humbert/theta-null splitting equations at window blocksize $w$ needs solving a structured Boolean/2-adic system in $e \approx \log_2 N$ variables in $L_N[\alpha < 1/3]$.
- **Missing lemma [SPECULATIVE]:** Show that the composed $e$-step genus-2 Richelot/theta-splitting ideal over $\mathbb{F}_{\ell^2}$, restricted to the 1-parameter norm torus $\mathcal{T}_e$, admits sub-$L_N[1/3]$ Gröbner/resultant decimation or mid-chain invariant pruning.
- **Pre-registered toy test & Python result [MEASURED]:**
  - *Pre-registered:* On 10 semiprimes $N \in [500, 5000]$ ($p, q \equiv 1 \pmod 3$): (P1a) verify Cornacchia setup $a = 2^e - mN$ and deterministic factoring from $(\nu_+, \nu_-)$ in $10/10$ cases; (P1b) test whether half-depth prefixes $\mathcal{T}_{\lfloor e/2 \rfloor}$ carry any group-automorphism or shortest-$\mathbb{Z}[\omega]$-coset-lift signal separating $\mu \nu_+$ from fake isotropic kernels.
  - *Result:* **P1a passed 10/10.** **P1b confirmed no local prefix leak:** $T_1(\mathbb{Z}/2^k\mathbb{Z})$ acts transitively on $\mathcal{T}_k$, and at $k = \lfloor e/2 \rfloor$ the true prefix's shortest global lift norm sits at mean percentile **$0.609$** (uniform noise), entering the bottom $5\%$ only at $k^*/e = 0.684 \in [0.58, 0.82]$ ($2^{2k} \gtrsim mN$). Any speedup must be global across the $e$-step Richelot equations.
- **$P(\alpha < 1/3 \text{ heuristic})$:** **$0.3\%$**.

